course: dictionary
lesson: 6589
title: Many meanings of no
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: The word no is tiny, but it has several jobs. It can mean not any, as in «No apples» meaning zero apples. It can be an answer, as in «Is it raining? No.» It can also mean that something is not allowed, as in «No running» on a sign.
explain: Context tells you which job it is doing. Look at the words next to it and ask: is it counting, answering a question, or giving a rule? In «Mia said «Okay, no worries» and didn't push», no is part of a friendly phrase that means it is fine.
explain: Sometimes no means not any in a more formal way. «Spinach gives no sudden muscles» means it gives none at all. Spinach is healthy, but muscles grow over months with exercise, food and rest, not from one bite.
fact: No means not any, or zero.
fact: No is the answer when something is not true or you do not agree.
fact: No can mean something is not allowed, as in «No entry».
fact: «No.» with a dot is short for number, as in «No. 5».
fact: Casual words like «nah», «nope» and «no worries» are everyday ways to say no, or to say it is fine; «no worries» is common in Australia and New Zealand.
exercise: «There are no apples left in the bowl.» What does no mean here? | Yes, please | Very quickly | A number, like No. 3 | *Not any, zero
exercise: «Is it going to rain?» «No.» What does no answer? | That it will rain loudly | *That it is not going to rain | That the sun is out | That you are late
exercise: A sign says «No entry». What does no mean? | Number three | Entry is free | *You are not allowed in | You must go in quickly
test: Mia said «Okay, no worries». What does no worries mean? | Please leave now | Stop and be very worried | *It's fine, don't worry | Worries are counted here
test: In «Room No. 9 is at the end of the hall», what does No. mean? | Short for not | A rule about rooms | *Short for number | A question about the hall
exam: Which sentence uses no to mean not any? | «Room No. 9 is at the end.» | *«We had no milk for breakfast.» | «No parking here after six.» | «No, I do not want to go.»
